      "text": "`entire enable --yes` is intended as a fully non-interactive end-to-end bootstrap: initialize Git, create a private GitHub repository under the user’s personal account with the directory name, use the default initial commit message, enable all available agents, accept telemetry, and confirm Vercel blocking; explicit flags such as `--agent`, `--no-github`, and `--telemetry=false` always take precedence.",
